                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "MOAI is another Time Management game from the guys over at Alawar. This time your character is stranded on an uncharted island and must work with a tribe of natives to restore their island and make your way back home.  It's a fun premise which is enhanced by storytelling sequences between each level and a simple narrative that adds some meat to an already enjoyable game.\n\nAs with other titles in the genre, the gameplay is pretty standard and consists of multi-tasking activites as efficiently as possible while managing resources to complete specific tasks (build, gather, etc.).  Coming up with the best strategy to complete the objectives in record time can be quite challenging, but not impossible once you determine your strategy and execute it well. If Gold (3 coins) is a little too stressful for you and you're wanting to go more casual, Silver is easily doable on most levels, and snagging Bronze a cinch.  I don't think you can fail a level without actively trying to fail it, so there's not a ton of pressure if you just want to play through for the story and artwork.\n\nAnd the artwork is indeed a reason to play through the game.  MOAI's presentation is REALLY well done.  The art has a nice hand painted look to it with high quality story CG's that are both colorful and creative.  The story narration is also full English voiced and the narrator nicely acted.  While the story itself seems a bit random at times, often being just enough to link each stage together, the writing is polished and even quite humorous.  Music-wise, I found the Disney-esque orchestral soundtrack a highlight, enough so that I wish there were a DLC or music tracks included as an extras, but I'll just have to live with listening to it while I play. \n\nWith full Steam integration including 53 Steam achievements, Trading Cards and Cloud Support, if you're a fan of the genre you really can't go wrong here. These things add a ton of value to any game on the platform, but for casual titles they're almost a must and are a very welcome addition.  MOAI is definitely one of the better Time Management games I've played and has handily exceeded my expectations. I will be sure to 100% this gem and enjoy every moment of it.\n\nBottom Line: Recommended for those who enjoy strategic, time-based gameplay, but will also appeal to more casual players with its storytelling and high level of polish.\n\n[code][h1]Curated by: [url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/33004802-Chudah%27s-Corner/]Chudah's Corner[/url][/h1][/code]",
